/> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mage Sight only shows how everything is devoid of purpose and meaning, how existence is constantly and unknowingly falling to the depths of the void, towards an absolute end. It is survival instinct highlighting what can be used to persevere. Increasing one's Gnosis represents how far one has climbed back to the surface, the Supernal, the true reality where one is safe and free.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Observation:</b> This is inspired by the game <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XzS6RwXC-eI&amp;t=186s&amp;quot;]The</a> Void[/URL], with the Brothers being the Manifest summons of Forces and the Sisters being the Recondite ones for Spirit.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>May I ask to come up with another one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T23:01:18-07:00","id":1481426,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Boddho, the Sundered Earthbound</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ruling Arcana:</b> Space and Life</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Inferior Arcanum:</b> Fate </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Quote:</b> <i>&quot;They want to overcome sickness, but can't bind things. The sorcerers' forefathers beheld it was about the dreadnoughts. They tore old binds, rightly. But no new ones were woven. So I come back.&quot;</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Watchtower is not one that can be Signed or Joined, but one Disembarks upon its Realm. It is perceived as a town built atop the Bull/Earth, houses are grown from its bones and trees are fed from its sweat. Atop it lies the Watchtower, piercing its back like a matador's estoque. It is said this representative of the Fall, with Atlanteans warping the natural order to suit humanity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The town is flooded with plague, a pestilence that seeks to winnow away this encroachment upon the Earth. It seeks to bind humanity to it once more, to create a one-from-many, subsume individuality and remove human's ability to impose their own order. Because of this, the strings of Fate are weakened here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Surviving in the town requires one to know how to coax herbs from the ground, create tinctures, endure fatigue and perform surgery. It requires the hands of a healer, which hold sway over Life.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Navigating it demands one to see the Lines, to understand how everything is bound. A skilled willworker is one who chooses how to mend or sever the Lines, isolating or opening sections of the town, weaving people together towards a single goal or confounding them away from it. In the end, the one who controls how the Space of the town is used shapes the future.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mage Sight reveals the pulse of the town, the blood flowing beneath it, the civilization that grows from it, how it takes a life of its own and people are part of the superorganism it creates. Increasing Gnosis allows one to become more apt at fighting the plague, with each Supernal revelation the mage comes ever closer to synthesizing the panacea within themselves, securing their claim to true agency once and for all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Observation:</b> This is heavily inspired by the game <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E7uKUgire7Y\" target=\"_blank\">Pathologic 2</a>, with the Tragedians being the summons of Space and Executors the ones for Life. The fact both are manifest summons is a reflection of how this Watchtower is not well put together, not &quot;sensibly bound&quot;. The Watchrower is not meant to be signed for any number of reasons. It could be a prototype of the real Imperial spell, a reflection of the real ones or even a representation of the God Machine and its intended role.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-19-2022, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T06:51:44-07:00","id":1481453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481205-lower-depths-watchtower-and-dur-abzu?p=1481426#post1481426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Boddho, the Sundered Earthbound</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ruling Arcana:</b> Space and Life</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Inferior Arcanum:</b> Fate </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Quote:</b> <i>&amp;quot;They want to overcome sickness, but can't bind things. The sorcerers' forefathers beheld it was about the dreadnoughts. They tore old binds, rightly. But no new ones were woven. So I come back.&amp;quot;</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Watchtower is not one that can be Signed or Joined, but one Disembarks upon its Realm. It is perceived as a town built atop the Bull/Earth, houses are grown from its bones and trees are fed from its sweat. Atop it lies the Watchtower, piercing its back like a matador's estoque. It is said this representative of the Fall, with Atlanteans warping the natural order to suit humanity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The town is flooded with plague, a pestilence that seeks to winnow away this encroachment upon the Earth. It seeks to bind humanity to it once more, to create a one-from-many, subsume individuality and remove human's ability to impose their own order. Because of this, the strings of Fate are weakened here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Surviving in the town requires one to know how to coax herbs from the ground, create tinctures, endure fatigue and perform surgery. It requires the hands of a healer, which hold sway over Life.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Navigating it demands one to see the Lines, to understand how everything is bound. A skilled willworker is one who chooses how to mend or sever the Lines, isolating or opening sections of the town, weaving people together towards a single goal or confounding them away from it. In the end, the one who controls how the Space of the town is used shapes the future.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mage Sight reveals the pulse of the town, the blood flowing beneath it, the civilization that grows from it, how it takes a life of its own and people are part of the superorganism it creates. Increasing Gnosis allows one to become more apt at fighting the plague, with each Supernal revelation the mage comes ever closer to synthesizing the panacea within themselves, securing their claim to true agency once and for all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Observation:</b> This is heavily inspired by the game <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E7uKUgire7Y&amp;quot;]Pathologic</a> 2[/URL], with the Tragedians being the summons of Space and Executors the ones for Life. The fact both are manifest summons is a reflection of how this Watchtower is not well put together, not &amp;quot;sensibly bound&amp;quot;. The Watchrower is not meant to be signed for any number of reasons. It could be a prototype of the real Imperial spell, a reflection of the real ones or even a representation of the God Machine and its intended role.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This so good!<br /> I don't suppose you could give some guidelines on your process? What I should keep in mind while wditing my own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T10:06:51-07:00","id":1481464,"title":"","content":"Thank you, glad you liked them. Since these are Watchtowers of the Lower Depths, first I try to make sure that whatever theme I choose gives a feeling of emptyness or hunger. Since they are analogous to Watchtowers, they need to provide a framework one can use to interpret reality and the Arcana, albeit an uneasy one. They cannot connect you to the Supernal via a lie, so instead they present uncomfortable truths. <br /> <br /> Turgor, for example, is about how everything erodes or becomes banal, including the self's dreams and spark of creativity, unless one has the drive and passion to climb to a better future. <br /> <br /> After presenting a brief overview of the themes, I move on to explain how the Ruling Arcana are seen within its point of view. That provides the general feel of what interacting with its Realm feels like.<br /> <br /> Expanding upon the Inferior Arcanum is a device to explain why being connected to this Watchtower is distressing. Turgor is probably probably pretty far from the Supernal, since Prime is the Arcanum magic uses to know and define itself (which is why none of the traditiona Path Realms have it as Inferior), so it creates dread by trying to consume that spark from the world. <br /> <br /> Boddho focuses on the fear of how these ecosystems (nature and civilization) create a web of connections that makes being in full control of our actions difficult, since what appears to be one choice pulls on the threads connecting everything and makes it so many other choices are made alongside them. An example is buying a tomato at a grocey store, which could end up supporting toxic pesticides, exploiting labour and global warming. You think you are making one choice, but are actually also unknowingly making dozens more and thoroughly researching everything all the time is impossible due to the complexity of it all.<br /> <br /> Mage Sight provides an basis for how the other Arcana and reality can be seen using this Watchtower. Its not as detailed as the sections in <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, but should be enough to establish a place to start expanding on the concept. <br /> <br /> The change in perspective with increasing Gnosis is used to further reinforce the themes and how delving deeper is seen as a way out of an unsettling situation. Would these create more Banishers ? Perhaps incentize the adoption of a more altruistic approach? Drive one to the Scelestus ways in desperation to escape ? Its all open to interpretation.<br /> <br /> Lastly, those two writeups specifically were heavily inspired by games from Ice Pick Lodge. Their worldbuilding and approach to symbolism tends to be excellent and the two games cited specifically resonate with the setting of Mage. They are brutally difficult, but thoughtfully crafted and very much worth the journey, so I recommend experiencing them as a source of inspiration. I am not sure if that also applies to their latest game, <i>Know By Heart</i>, since I haven't had the chance to play it yet, but I think <i>The Void</i>, <i>Pathologic 2</i> (which is a far superior remake/sequel to the first) and perhaps <i>Knock Knock</i> should be pretty safe bets.<br /> <br /> That would be the general outline of how I went about the process, hope it helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-19-2022, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T15:23:14-07:00","id":1537769,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>, any chance you can make a third one? For old time's sake <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T20:20:45-07:00","id":1537781,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Jantek\u00f8ben, The Outgrowing Metropolis</span></b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcana: </b>Matter &amp; Space<br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum:</b> Time<br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>&quot;We were all of us cogs in a great machine which sometimes rolled forward, nobody knew where, sometimes backwards, nobody knew why.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Perceiving this Watchtower is a sign it has started to Integrate the visitor. Its denizens are obsessive automatons, devoted only to the expansion of the metropolis, following the corrupted guidelines of a nameless architect. In order to avoid becoming a drone, one must understand its mechanisms, learning to wield the Matter around oneself and control the myriad apparatuses that regulate the city's infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Unorthodox constructions dot the landscapes. With stairways leading to nowhere, skyscrapers hanging from the ceiling like stalactites and even gravity defying rooms. Learning to navigate it requires one to recognize each liminal Space for what it is, establishing waypoints and leveraging its unique laws to bypass obstacles.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, the constant renovations means no marks the individual makes on the city remains for long, in the end, all traces of their history in the city are erased. Windows and clocks are nearly nonexistent, and whatever music is found consists only of repetitive loops, making in difficult for one to tell the flow of Time.<br /> <br /> Mage Sight the constant grind of a Rube Goldberg machine that seeks only to perpetuate itself, crushing any ambitions that do not match its own. Increasing one's Gnosis represents a greater understanding of the systems, allowing one to affect permanent change upon the city, with the Supernal having the master controls.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation:</b> This is inspired by the city from <i>Blame</i>, the city of Cloudbank from <i>Transistor</i>, as well as the worst aspects of the Law of Jante. The quote is by Ernst Toller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-22-2024, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T21:56:10-07:00","id":1537784,"title":"","content":"Thanks man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T22:36:26-07:00","id":1537787,"title":"","content":"No prob. Unfortunately I went to fix a typo and now the post has now vanished until approved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T22:39:22-07:00","id":1537788,"title":"","content":"Oh that happens to me sometime too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T16:06:50-07:00","id":1537883,"title":"","content":"Re-posting, since I think my last one was lost when the forums were down:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Jantek\u00f8ben, The Outgrowing Metropolis</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcana: </b>Matter &amp; Space<br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum: </b>Time<br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>&quot;We were all of us cogs in a great machine which sometimes rolled forward, nobody knew where, sometimes backwards, nobody knew why.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Perceiving this city is a sign it has started to Integrate the visitor. Its denizens are obsessive automatons, devoted only to the expansion of the metropolis, following the corrupted guidelines of a nameless architect. In order to avoid becoming a drone, one must understand these mechanisms, learning to wield the Matter around oneself and control the myriad apparatuses that regulate the city's infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Unorthodox constructions dot the landscapes. With stairways leading to nowhere, skyscrapers hanging from the ceiling like stalagtites and even gravity defying rooms. Learning to navigate it requires one to recognize each liminal Space for what it is, establishing waypoints and leveraging their unique laws to bypass obstacles.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, the constant renovations means no marks the individual makes on the city remains for long, in the end, all traces of their history in the city are erased. Windows and clocks are nearly nonexistent, and whatever music is found consists only of repetitive loops, making in difficult for one to tell the flow of Time.<br /> <br /> Mage Sight the constant grind of a Rube Goldberg machine that seeks only to perpetuate itself, crushing any ambitions that do not match its own. Increasing one's Gnosis represents achieving a greater holistic understanding of the systems, reprogramming its fabricators and allowing one to make permanent changes upon the city, with the Supernal holding the master control.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation:</b> This is inspired by the city from <i>Blame</i>, the Cloudbank from <i>Transistor</i>, as well as the worst aspects of the Law of Jante. The quote is by Ernst Toller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}